-- title:
--   From pro-representability to algebra maps into complete local rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and write $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ for `Zp2 q`, the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements. Let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, complete with respect to the ideal generated by the image of $q$, this ideal being maximal, and with algebraically closed residue field $k$; let $\iota:\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}\to O^{nr}$ be a ring map and $X_0$ a formal $O_D$-module over $k$ for the reduction $(\mathrm{res}\circ\iota)$ — that is, a commutative two-dimensional formal group law with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ by $2$-tuples of power series and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\mathrm{Frob}\,a]\circ\varpi$ — whose Lie algebra splits into two complementary invertible submodules (`IsSpecial`) and whose $[q]$ has kernel of degree $q^4$ (`HasHeight 4`). Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, with $\mathrm{res}_R:R\to k$ compatible with the residue map of $O^{nr}$, let $X_u$ be a formal $O_D$-module over $R$, and $w_u$ an isomorphism $X_u\otimes_R k\cong X_0$. Assume the pro-representability hypothesis: for every Artinian local $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjection $\mathrm{res}_A:A\to k$ compatible with the residue map, every formal $O_D$-module $X$ over $A$ that is special for $(A\text{-structure})\circ\iota$ and of height $4$, and every isomorphism $w:X\otimes_A k\cong X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra map $\chi:R\to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi=\mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v:X_u\otimes_{R,\chi}A\cong X$ whose reduction composed with $w$ has the same underlying series as $w_u$. Let further $B'$ be a Noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_{B'}:B'\to k$ compatible with the residue map, $X'$ a formal $O_D$-module over $B'$ and $w'$ an isomorphism $X'\otimes_{B'}k\cong X_0$. The conclusion is that there exists an $O^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi:R\to B'$ with $\mathrm{res}_{B'}\circ\chi=\mathrm{res}_R$ such that for every $n>0$ there is an isomorphism $v$ between $X_u$ base changed along $R\to B'\to B'/\mathfrak m_{B'}^n$ and $X'\otimes_{B'}B'/\mathfrak m_{B'}^n$ satisfying, for every ring map $B'/\mathfrak m_{B'}^n\to k$ factoring $\mathrm{res}_{B'}$, the compatibility $w'\circ v = w_u$ on underlying series. No uniqueness of $\chi$ is asserted, and the isomorphism is produced only modulo each power of the maximal ideal, not over $B'$ itself.
--
--   This is the "deformation gives a point" direction of pro-representability for deformations of a special formal $O_D$-module of height $4$ in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: a deformation over an arbitrary complete Noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra is classified, level by level in the maximal-adic filtration, by an $O^{nr}$-algebra map out of the pro-representing ring. It is applied, together with explicit families over $O^{nr}[[T]]$ and $O^{nr}[[U,V]]/(UV-q)$, to produce surjections from the pro-representing ring onto those models; the Artinian input is supplied by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.isSpecial_and_hasHeight_four_of_isIso_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.isSpecial_and_hasHeight_four_of_isIso_of_isArtinianRing).
